WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The store controls vendor access
Tenant → Carriers shows whether vendor labels are Allowed or Off for
each connected carrier. An authorized operator reviews and confirms a
change; it does not erase existing labels or cancel bookings.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Choose a named carrier on the shipment
Tenant → Shipments → Labels lists only eligible connected carriers. The
local test choice needs no uploaded file: Generate label creates a
private sample PDF. A manual carrier still requires the actual label
file.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Vendors choose from the store-approved list
Vendor → Shipping → owned shipment → Add label replaces numeric carrier
IDs with names. Only carriers enabled for this store and vendor label
use appear. Ask the store operator when the list is empty; do not enter
another store’s shipment.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Read the result and keep dispatch separate
The saved row shows TEST, its tracking reference and a download link.
Opening the private sample was verified locally. Repeating the same
carrier label reuses the saved result. Label generation alone leaves the
shipment Pending; real dispatch needs its separate authorized update.
